A||||5||DecadenceR||84 and 85+||||5||
Z||000000||DecadenceR||05-28-2001||08:03 PM||||Does anyone know the differences between the 84 four-banger and the rest of the years?<BR>I look up all kinda stuff, and everything fits the 85+ motors, and 85+ bodies...<BR>Very frustrating.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Iron Duke Wellingsley||05-28-2001||08:28 PM||||The 84s are different in a few ways.  The most significant is the wiring, totally different.<P>84s have no third brake light, glass sail panels, a vented decklid with smooth deck panels, and some other little stuff.<P>The 84-87 Fieros share chassis and suspension, but the 85-87 models have the V6 engine.  <P>Most parts that fit in a 85 will fit in an 84 too, though the engine wiring connectors are different so ignition components require some electrical engineering to use.<P>I have an 84 and there are tons of modifications possible on first year cars.  Engine swaps are a lot harder, but they can be done too.  <P>What do you want on your car???? ||||reg||7
Z||000002||DecadenceR||05-29-2001||08:46 AM||||Well, I had purchased an Accel coil and it was supposed to fit on my car... Turns out after I went though the pain of taking the old one off, the new one has a totally different wire connector. Would I be able to switch to the updated wire connector?<BR>But basically I'm looking for anything to improve the performance a little bit.<p>[This message has been edited by DecadenceR (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||05-29-2001||05:10 PM||||*bump*||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnt671||05-29-2001||06:25 PM||||I had the same problem with mt 84 when I changed to an msd blaster coil.  Went to the junkyard and found a car with the newer typle connetions and spliced the later model connectors into the car.  The wire colors were even the some. I forget what model I got them off but any 85 or so gm duke 4 cyl should have the some setup.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Iron Duke Wellingsley||05-29-2001||10:47 PM||||I have the Accel coil on my 84, but it is connected to a MSD 6AL ignition.  <P>This combination of parts is really easy to wire up.  Without the MSD, it is not so easy.<P>Probably the connector swap from an 85 or 86 is the easy way.  Or, just spend $150 and get the MSD ignition too.  The ignition system on my car makes sparks that are huge and beautiful.  If you leave the plug wire off of the Accel, then the sparks leap from the terminal to the trunk wall of the engine compartment.  It's something to see, indeed.<P>Before I bought the MSD, I fried my ignition control unit trying to wire up the Accel coil.  I could not tell you how to do this though I believe it's possible.<P>If you want to use the MSD ignition, then just connect the red wire (looked pink to me) and the black wire with pink stripe to the red wire on the MSD.  The other two wires go to the white wire on the MSD.  The MSD comes with directions, wiring diagrams, and all the parts you need.  <P>The MSD can mount in the trunk just to the left of the trunk light.  Then, the wiring goes through the trunk just to the right of the trunk light.  It's a straight run from there to the distributor.  I put the Accel coil above the canister on the engine side of the trunk wall.  <P>It looks trick!  Email me if you want pictures or more info.  <BR> ||||reg||1
